From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gcc: fix C++17 bool increment bootstrap failure

Modern host compilers reject ++ on bool in C++17 mode. GCC 4.8.5 still
contains one such use in reload1.c. The field is used as a boolean flag, so
assigning true preserves the effective behavior while allowing the old
compiler to bootstrap on modern hosts.
---
 gcc/reload1.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/reload1.c b/gcc/reload1.c
index b05f43f..561837e 100644
--- a/gcc/reload1.c
+++ b/gcc/reload1.c
@@ -440,7 +440,7 @@ init_reload (void)
 
   while (memory_address_p (QImode, tem))
     {
-      spill_indirect_levels++;
+      spill_indirect_levels = true;
       tem = gen_rtx_MEM (Pmode, tem);
     }
 
